/* Valid: r = 0.5 is a witness, and P holds at every non-negative real.  No
   integer is a witness, so a search for the existential's witness among the
   integers finds none and refutes a problem that is not this one: that
   refutation must not be printed as invalid.  With an integer witness
   (r + r = 2) the same search succeeds. */
exists (r: real). r + r = 1.0 /\ P r
s.t.
P (x: real): bool =nu x >= 0.0;
